s\0A * usually come first as they tend to be configuration parameters.\0A * Refer to the documentation of each key derivation or key agreement\0A * algorithm for information.\0A *\0A * This function is used for inputs which are fixed-size non-negative\0A * integers.\0A *\0A * If this function returns an error status, the operation enters an error\0A * state and must be aborted by calling psa_key_derivation_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation       The key derivation operation object to use.\0A *                                It must have been set up with\0A *                                psa_key_derivation_setup() and must not\0A *                                have produced any output yet.\0A * \5Cparam step                    Which step the input data is for.\0A * \5Cparam[in] value               The value of the numeric input.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         \5Cc step is not compatible with the operation's algorithm, or\0A *         \5Cc step does not allow numeric inputs.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_HARDWARE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid for this input \5Cp step, or\0A *         the library has not been previously initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_key_derivation_input_integer(\0A    psa_key_derivation_operation_t *operation,\0A    psa_key_derivation_step_t step,\0A    uint64_t value);\0A\0A/** Provide an input for key derivation in the form of a key.\0A *\0A * Which inputs are required and in what order depends on the algorithm.\0A * Refer to the documentation of each key derivation or key agreement\0A * algorithm for information.\0A *\0A * This function obtains input from a key object, which is usually correct for\0A * secret inputs or for non-secret personalization strings kept in the key\0A * store. To pass a non-secret parameter which is not in the key store,\0A * call psa_key_derivation_input_bytes() instead of this function.\0A * Refer to the documentation of individual step types\0A * (`PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_xxx` values of type ::psa_key_derivation_step_t)\0A * for more information.\0A *\0A * If this function returns an error status, the operation enters an error\0A * state and must be aborted by calling psa_key_derivation_abort().\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation       The key derivation operation object to use.\0A *                                It must have been set up with\0A *                                psa_key_derivation_setup() and must not\0A *                                have produced any output yet.\0A * \5Cparam step                    Which step the input data is for.\0A * \5Cparam key                     Identifier of the key. It must have an\0A *                                appropriate type for step and must allow the\0A *                                usage #PSA_KEY_USAGE_DERIVE or\0A *                                #PSA_KEY_USAGE_VERIFY_DERIVATION (see note)\0A *                                and the algorithm used by the operation.\0A *\0A * \5Cnote Once all inputs steps are completed, the operations will allow:\0A * - psa_key_derivation_output_bytes() if each input was either a direct input\0A *   or  a key with #PSA_KEY_USAGE_DERIVE set;\0A * - psa_key_derivation_output_key() or psa_key_derivation_output_key_custom()\0A *   if the input for step\0A *   #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_SECRET or #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_PASSWORD\0A *   was from a key slot with #PSA_KEY_USAGE_DERIVE and each other input was\0A *   either